{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"examples","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Examples"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Want to skip to the implementation? Check out these examples:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/ranger/latest/docs/framework/react/examples/basic","children":[{"type":"text","value":"basic"}]}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The API below described how to use the "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"basic"}]},{"type":"text","value":" features."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"values","children":[{"type":"text","value":"values"}]},{"type":"code","value":"values: ReadonlyArray<number>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"text","value":" The current value (or values) for the range."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"min","children":[{"type":"text","value":"min"}]},{"type":"code","value":"min: number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"text","value":" The minimum limit for the range."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"max","children":[{"type":"text","value":"max"}]},{"type":"code","value":"max: number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"text","value":" The maximum limit for the range."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"stepsize","children":[{"type":"text","value":"stepSize"}]},{"type":"code","value":"stepSize: number","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Required"}]},{"type":"text","value":" The distance between selectable steps."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"onchange","children":[{"type":"text","value":"onChange"}]},{"type":"code","value":"onChange: (instance: Ranger<TTrackElement>) => void","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A function that is called when the handle is released."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"handles","children":[{"type":"text","value":"handles"}]},{"type":"code","value":"handles: ReadonlyArray<{\n  value: number\n  isActive: boolean\n  onKeyDownHandler(event): function\n  onMouseDownHandler(event): function\n  onTouchStart(event): function\n}>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Handles to be rendered. Each "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"handle"},{"type":"text","value":" has the following props:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value: number"},{"type":"text","value":" - The current value for the handle."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isActive: boolean"},{"type":"text","value":" - Denotes if the handle is currently being dragged."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onKeyDownHandler(event): func"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onMouseDownHandler(event): func"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onTouchStart(event): func"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"activehandleindex","children":[{"type":"text","value":"activeHandleIndex"}]},{"type":"code","value":"activeHandleIndex: null | number","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The zero-based index of the handle that is currently being dragged, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":" if no handle is being dragged."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"examples","text":"Examples","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"values","text":"values","level":3},{"id":"min","text":"min","level":3},{"id":"max","text":"max","level":3},{"id":"stepsize","text":"stepSize","level":3},{"id":"onchange","text":"onChange","level":3},{"id":"api","text":"API","level":2},{"id":"handles","text":"handles","level":3},{"id":"activehandleindex","text":"activeHandleIndex","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n## Examples\n\nWant to skip to the implementation? Check out these examples:\n\n- [basic](/ranger/latest/docs/framework/react/examples/basic)\n\nThe API below described how to use the **basic** features.\n\n## Options\n\n### values\n\n```tsx\nvalues: ReadonlyArray<number>\n```\n\n**Required** The current value (or values) for the range.\n\n### min\n\n```tsx\nmin: number\n```\n\n**Required** The minimum limit for the range.\n\n### max\n\n```tsx\nmax: number\n```\n\n**Required** The maximum limit for the range.\n\n### stepSize\n\n```ts\nstepSize: number\n```\n\n**Required** The distance between selectable steps.\n\n### onChange\n\n```ts\nonChange: (instance: Ranger<TTrackElement>) => void\n```\n\nA function that is called when the handle is released.\n\n## API\n\n### handles\n\n```tsx\nhandles: ReadonlyArray<{\n  value: number\n  isActive: boolean\n  onKeyDownHandler(event): function\n  onMouseDownHandler(event): function\n  onTouchStart(event): function\n}>\n```\n\nHandles to be rendered. Each `handle` has the following props:\n\n- `value: number` - The current value for the handle.\n- `isActive: boolean` - Denotes if the handle is currently being dragged.\n- `onKeyDownHandler(event): func`\n- `onMouseDownHandler(event): func`\n- `onTouchStart(event): func`\n\n### activeHandleIndex\n\n```tsx\nactiveHandleIndex: null | number\n```\n\nThe zero-based index of the handle that is currently being dragged, or `null` if no handle is being dragged.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nname: Basic\nroute: /api/basic\nmenu: API\n---\n\n## Examples\n\nWant to skip to the implementation? Check out these examples:\n\n- [basic](/ranger/latest/docs/framework/react/examples/basic)\n\nThe API below described how to use the **basic** features.\n\n## Options\n\n### values\n\n```tsx\nvalues: ReadonlyArray<number>\n```\n\n**Required** The current value (or values) for the range.\n\n### min\n\n```tsx\nmin: number\n```\n\n**Required** The minimum limit for the range.\n\n### max\n\n```tsx\nmax: number\n```\n\n**Required** The maximum limit for the range.\n\n### stepSize\n\n```ts\nstepSize: number\n```\n\n**Required** The distance between selectable steps.\n\n### onChange\n\n```ts\nonChange: (instance: Ranger<TTrackElement>) => void\n```\n\nA function that is called when the handle is released.\n\n## API\n\n### handles\n\n```tsx\nhandles: ReadonlyArray<{\n  value: number\n  isActive: boolean\n  onKeyDownHandler(event): function\n  onMouseDownHandler(event): function\n  onTouchStart(event): function\n}>\n```\n\nHandles to be rendered. Each `handle` has the following props:\n\n- `value: number` - The current value for the handle.\n- `isActive: boolean` - Denotes if the handle is currently being dragged.\n- `onKeyDownHandler(event): func`\n- `onMouseDownHandler(event): func`\n- `onTouchStart(event): func`\n\n### activeHandleIndex\n\n```tsx\nactiveHandleIndex: null | number\n```\n\nThe zero-based index of the handle that is currently being dragged, or `null` if no handle is being dragged.\n"}
